215	   215	# Two things a hack asks of filled triangles that TinyGL stores but ignores.
216	   216	#
217	   217	# Polygon offset: glPolygonOffset and GL_POLYGON_OFFSET_FILL are recorded and
218	   218	# nothing reads them, so a line drawn on the edge of its own filled polygon
219	   219	# fights it for the depth test. The offset is factor * the polygon's steepest
220	   220	# depth slope + units * the smallest depth step, pushed away from the viewer.
221	   221	# The rasteriser also snaps a polygon's vertices to whole pixels, so its depth
222	   222	# at a pixel can be wrong by a pixel's slope in each direction, which the
223	   223	# hack's own numbers assume away: when an offset is asked for, that margin
224	   224	# (|dz/dx| + |dz/dy|) is added. Without it the polygon still erased a few
225	   225	# percent of its own line, a different few each frame, which flickered.
