622	+/* Times a push to the panel's refresh. The AMOLED scans its memory top to
623	+ * bottom 60 times a second, and a full push takes about two refreshes, so a
624	+ * push that starts at a random moment shows two pictures at once, with a seam
625	+ * between them: a thin line that moved a few pixels can fall in the gap and
626	+ * vanish for a frame. The panel's TE line pulses once a refresh. Starting a
627	+ * push at the same point in every cycle puts the seam where it is chosen, and
628	+ * the right point keeps the write ahead of the scan so there is none.
629	+ *
630	+ * An interrupt feeds it the edges of TE with the microsecond they arrived; the
631	+ * main loop asks how long to wait. Times are 32-bit microseconds that may
632	+ * wrap. */
633	+typedef struct {
634	+  volatile uint32_t last_rise_us;
635	+  volatile uint32_t period_us; /* 0 until two rising edges one period apart */
636	+  volatile uint32_t rises;     /* rising edges accepted, saturating at 2 */
637	+  uint32_t offset_us;
638	+  uint32_t timeout_us;
